// Indestructible = an event-side can't-happen [CR#702.12b,614.17]: the
// `Destroy(this)` keyword action simply cannot occur. Reads like the card
// ("can't be destroyed") and covers both destroy causes ([CR#701.8b]) —
// the effect destroy AND the lethal-damage SBA, which both perform the Destroy
// keyword action. Naturally ignores a toughness-0 / lethal-state MOVE
// ([CR#704.5f], a plain `Move`, not the Destroy atom) and sacrifice
// ([CR#701.21a]) — neither is a Destroy keyword action, so no cause-predicate
// is needed. The engine's cant pass ([CR#614.17]) in `apply_occurrence`
// suppresses the Destroy `Act` event before `apply` runs — the replacement
// registry is skipped entirely ([CR#614.17c]).
KeywordAbility(
    name: "Indestructible",
    template: "indestructible",
    abilities: [Static(CantHappen(Destroy(Ref(This))))],
)
